== C. rearrangement: a 40-bin histogram error law and a bin permutation of it (same masses, other places)
   histogram      RMS 0.7237  mean|e| 0.6440  max 1.6890 | h = 1.2988 bits | rate - (h - log2 Delta) at Delta = w/64: 0.0001, w/8: 0.0010 | rate at w/2: 5.8686, 1: 1.5866, coarse (Delta = 2L): 0.5285
   bins permuted  RMS 0.9830  mean|e| 0.8500  max 1.6890 | h = 1.2988 bits | rate - (h - log2 Delta) at Delta = w/64: 0.0031, w/8: 0.0246 | rate at w/2: 5.9629, 1: 1.9684, coarse (Delta = 2L): 0.7235
   (as Delta -> 0 both rates approach h - log2 Delta = H(bins) + log2(w/Delta), and h is the same; the permutation
    changes the rate only through the smoothing at bin edges, O(Delta/w) bits; at coarser Delta the rates differ,
    and the coarse rate (1/Delta) int H2(F) sees where the mass is, at scales up to Delta)

